<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  CyberpunkVRPort. Take photo mode off the pad, leave it on the keyboard.

  WHY. The game binds TogglePhotoModeButton to IK_N and to IK_PAD_LR_THUMB, and that second one is
  both stick clicks inside a 0.1 s window. This port synthesises LEFT_THUMB for sprint (XInput.cpp,
  wantSprint) and RIGHT_THUMB for the right stick down crouch gesture (wantCrouch), and it emits
  them in the SAME FRAME, so the window is no protection at all -- sliding sends the game exactly
  that chord and photo mode opens on its own. The screen goes flat, camera controls appear, and the
  way out is not obvious in a headset.

  WHY THE BINDING AND NOT A BUTTON. Suppressing the two clicks from co-occurring was the first idea
  and it is wrong: sprint plus crouch IS the slide, so that trade buys a fix by removing a move the
  player wants. R3 cannot go either, because it carries the crouch gesture and also QuickMelee,
  Tag, Dive and PickUpBodyFromTakedown. The chord is the only part nobody asked for.

  N still opens photo mode, and ExitPhotoModeButton keeps IK_Escape, IK_N and IK_Pad_B_CIRCLE, so
  anyone already inside it can still get out with Circle.

  NOTE ON STYLE: no double hyphen anywhere in these comments. XML forbids it inside a comment and
  the game parser swallows that quietly, which is the worst way to be wrong.

  VERIFIED 2026-08-26. input_loader REPLACES on a name collision; it does not append. Measured in
  the merged r6\cache\inputUserMappings.xml after one launch: exactly ONE TogglePhotoModeButton
  mapping, carrying only IK_N, and no mapping anywhere still binds IK_PAD_LR_THUMB. Confirmed in
  play -- clicking both sticks no longer opens photo mode. Slide is unaffected, since nothing about
  sprint or crouch was touched.

  The IK_PAD_LR_THUMB buttonGroup itself still EXISTS in the cache. That is correct and is not a
  leftover: it is the chord's declaration, not a binding. Nothing maps to it any more.

  Escape hatch confirmed intact in the same read: ExitPhotoModeButton still carries IK_Escape, IK_N
  and IK_Pad_B_CIRCLE, so anyone who reaches photo mode by any other route still leaves with Circle.
-->
<bindings>
	<mapping name="TogglePhotoModeButton" type="Button">
		<button id="IK_N" overridableUI="photoMode" />
	</mapping>
</bindings>
